1. What is tee?

tee is used when you want to:

see command output on the screen AND save the same output into a file.

Think of it like a T-junction:

                 ┌──> Screen
Command Output ──┤
                 └──> File

Normally:

ls -l

shows output only on the screen.

With tee:

ls -l | tee files.txt

you get the output:

on the screen
saved in files.txt

Lab 1: Basic tee

Run:

mkdir ~/tee-lab
cd ~/tee-lab

Now:

ls -l | tee files.txt

Check the file:

